"""register_11nov_n1v3d.py -- records the v3c joint result (#128) with the order-of-events note, and registers v3d (the founder's release-day decay
hypothesis) BEFORE it runs. Idempotent.    python scripts_applied/register_11nov_n1v3d.py"""
import json
from pathlib import Path
j = {(r["family"], r["index"], r["direction"]): r for r in json.loads(Path("docs/news_events_v3_joint.json").read_text())}
def cell(k): r = j.get(k); return f"{r['mean_rank_corr']:+.3f} (p {r['p']:.4f}; before 2020 {r['before_2020']:+.3f}, from 2020 {r['from_2020']:+.3f})" if r else "not testable"
a, b = j[("all", "SOX", "fall")], j[("all", "SOX", "rise")]; both05 = a["p"] < 0.05 and b["p"] < 0.05 and a["mean_rank_corr"] > 0 and b["mean_rank_corr"] > 0; one0125 = min(a["p"], b["p"]) < 0.0125
ROWS = f"""| 2026-11-11 | v3c joint size test (primary: all documents; bar p < 0.0125) | SOX fall {cell(('all', 'SOX', 'fall'))}; SOX rise {cell(('all', 'SOX', 'rise'))}; SPX fall {cell(('all', 'SPX', 'fall'))}; SPX rise not testable. **Neither semiconductor group clears 0.0125**; both are below 0.05. Measured beside it, not judged: Fed documents only — SOX fall {cell(('fed', 'SOX', 'fall'))}, SOX rise {cell(('fed', 'SOX', 'rise'))}; BLS only — SOX fall {cell(('bls', 'SOX', 'fall'))}, SOX rise {cell(('bls', 'SOX', 'rise'))}. Five-session reversal return by third of the score (window 5, all documents), SOX fall: lowest −2.25%, middle +2.73%, highest +1.42% (n 121) — not a steady rise with the score; the clear feature is that when the documents lean WITH the fall, the fall continues. **Order of events, stated:** `record_11nov_n1v3a.py` (which carries this test's registration and prior #128) crashed on an import before writing its rows, and the joint test then ran. The registration text was nonetheless committed inside that script at 80c952a, before the result commit 70b6e54; the rows were written afterwards by rerunning the script with PYTHONPATH set. | **#128 {'right' if (both05 and one0125) else 'wrong (counted)'}** — both positive below 0.05 as predicted, but {'one clears' if one0125 else 'neither clears'} 0.0125. Reading: a tilt exists in semiconductors on the registered test's evidence at the 0.05 level only; the Fed-documents-after-a-fall cell (p 0.001) is a secondary cut and needs its own registered test — v3d makes Fed documents a primary family. |
| 2026-11-11 | **Caveat on what v3a–v3c measured (Claude)** | The reversal return ran over the sessions after the event day and the documents were released INSIDE those sessions, so the link is largely same-period (the document's release-day reaction is inside the return), not a forecast. It says documents and snap-backs go together; it does not yet say that reading the document lets one trade what follows. v3d separates the two. | — |
| 2026-11-11 | **v3d registered before running — release-day decay (founder's hypothesis)** | Founder, 11 Nov: "the news has its strongest effect the day it is released, then day by day the effect weakens — test whether the rebound on reverse news is largest on day 0 and weakens later." Everything re-aligned on the document's release day. Pairs = (event, document day) inside the 10-session window; score = −(event sign) × the day's mean equity implication. Per index × direction × family: **(a) day-0** rank correlation with the release-day return (one-sided); **(b) decay** = day 0 minus the mean of days +1…+5 (one-sided); **(c) drift** = rank correlation with the cumulative return over days +1…+5 — the only part still tradeable by someone who reads the document at the close of day 0 (one-sided); **(d) placebo** = days −2, −1 before the document, which a document cannot cause (two-sided; non-zero means the score reflects what prices had already done, or hindsight in the reader). Null: 2,000 shuffles of the scores across document days. Primary cells: SOX fall and SOX rise × families **all** and **Fed**; bar **p < 0.0125**. Returns by third of the score reported in percent. Limits stated: daily closes only — the minutes after a release are not visible; day 0 close-to-close contains the release for every document type. Priors: **#129** day-0 is positive with p < 0.0125 for Fed documents after SOX falls, and positive with p < 0.05 for all documents after SOX falls. **#130** decay is positive in both SOX-fall primary cells (the founder's hypothesis holds in direction), and the drift over days +1…+5 is NOT distinguishable from zero (p > 0.05) in all four primary cells — the effect is on the day, little is left after. **#131** the placebo is small, |mean| < 0.08, in all four primary cells. | — |
"""
TRACK = f"""
### 3.48 N1 v3c result; v3d registered (11 Nov 15:20)
Joint size test: SOX fall {a['mean_rank_corr']:+.3f} (p {a['p']:.3f}), SOX rise {b['mean_rank_corr']:+.3f} (p {b['p']:.3f}) — below 0.05, above the 0.0125 bar; #128 {'right' if (both05 and one0125) else 'counted wrong'}. Secondary: Fed documents after SOX falls +0.224 (p 0.001), stronger from 2020. Caveat recorded: v3a–c measured a same-period link, not a forecast. Founder's hypothesis (strongest on the release day, fading after) registered as v3d with day-0 / decay / drift / placebo tests, priors #129–#131. App question (score a document at release and show it on the site) parked until v3d says whether anything is left after day 0. Record-script crash and order of events stated in prereg_news_events.
"""
p = Path("docs/prereg_news_events.md"); s = p.read_text()
if "v3d registered before running" in s: print("  prereg_news_events: v3d already registered -- skipped")
else: p.write_text(s.rstrip("\n") + "\n" + ROWS); print("  prereg_news_events: v3c result (#128) recorded; v3d registered (#129-#131)")
t = Path("docs/TRACK.md"); s = t.read_text()
if "### 3.48 N1 v3c result" in s: print("  TRACK: 3.48 already present -- skipped")
else: t.write_text(s.rstrip("\n") + "\n" + TRACK); print("  TRACK: 3.48 appended")
